t-performance#Chat message-list rendering performance#Block flow, not a flex column","file":"lat.md/chat-performance","line":130},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/ChatInput.tsx","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-performance#Chat message-list rendering performance#Textarea auto-resize avoids per-keystroke reflow","file":"lat.md/chat-performance","line":138},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/virtualSlashCommands.ts#createSlashCommandVirtualLayout","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-performance#Chat message-list rendering performance#Slash command palette uses fixed-row virtualization","file":"lat.md/chat-performance","line":146},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/ChatInput.tsx","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-performance#Chat message-list rendering performance#Slash command palette uses fixed-row virtualization","file":"lat.md/chat-performance","line":150},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useDashboardChatTransport.ts#useDashboardChatTransport","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-performance#Chat message-list rendering performance#Table-heavy transcript heap profile","file":"lat.md/chat-performance","line":160},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useDashboardChatTransport.test.tsx","fromSection":"lat.md/chat-performance#Chat message-list rendering performance#Table-heavy transcript heap profile","file":"lat.md/chat-performance","line":160}],"paragraphs":[{"markdown":"Typing must stay fast no matter how long the conversation is. Layout cost is bounded by CSS containment plus one batched textarea measurement; React-tree cost by transcript windowing and coalesced streaming commits (issue #748).","startLine":3,"endLine":3,"text":"Typing must stay fast no matter how long the conversation is. Layout cost is bounded by CSS containment plus one batched textarea measurement; React-tree cost by transcript windowing and coalesced streaming commits (issue #748)."},{"markdown":"The symptom this guards against: in conversations with many messages, each keystroke took up to ~2.6s with an empty JS profile — the cost was entirely in Chromium's layout engine, recalculating the whole transcript on every keystroke. CPU and memory were normal; new sessions were instant. CSS containment fixed the layout half; the React half (reconciling every row on every streaming delta) is fixed by the windowing and delta coalescing described below.","startLine":5,"endLine":5,"text":"The symptom this guards against: in conversations with many messages, each keystroke took up to ~2.6s with an empty JS profile — the cost was entirely in Chromium's layout engine, recalculating the whole transcript on every keystroke. CPU and memory were normal; new sessions were instant. CSS containment fixed the layout half; the React half (reconciling every row on every streaming delta) is fixed by the windowing and delta coalescing described below."},{"markdown":"Long transcripts start with the newest [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/MessageList.tsx#TRANSCRIPT_WINDOW]] rows (100). Earlier rows collapse behind a \"Show N earlier messages\" button, bounding mounted rows while following output.","startLine":9,"endLine":9,"text":"Long transcripts start with the newest src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/MessageList.tsx#TRANSCRIPT_WINDOW rows (100). Earlier rows collapse behind a \"Show N earlier messages\" button, bounding mounted rows while following output."},{"markdown":"The window cut is computed per render in [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/MessageList.tsx]] with the following constraints:","startLine":11,"endLine":11,"text":"The window cut is computed per render in src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/MessageList.tsx with the following constraints:"},{"markdown":"**Never slice out the newest bubble.** The newest visible bubble owns the last-row marker (active avatar, approval bar), so the cut clamps to its index even when a longer-than-window run of reasoning/tool rows trails it.","startLine":13,"endLine":13,"text":"Never slice out the newest bubble. The newest visible bubble owns the last-row marker (active avatar, approval bar), so the cut clamps to its index even when a longer-than-window run of reasoning/tool rows trails it."},{"markdown":"**Don't split a tool run — within a bound.** The cut nudges back to the start of a contiguous tool_call/tool_result run so a ToolActivityGroup isn't cut in half, but the walk is bounded to one window: a pathological run of hundreds of tool rows splits at the bound instead of re-mounting the whole transcript (which would silently defeat the cap for exactly the agentic sessions #748 targets).","startLine":14,"endLine":14,"text":"Don't split a tool run — within a bound. The cut nudges back to the start of a contiguous tool_call/tool_result run so a ToolActivityGroup isn't cut in half, but the walk is bounded to one window: a pathological run of hundreds of tool rows splits at the bound instead of re-mounting the whole transcript (which would silently defeat the cap for exactly the agentic sessions #748 targets)."},{"markdown":"**Don't fake a turn at the cut.** Avatar grouping consults the hidden row just above the cut (`beforeWindow`), so a mid-turn cut doesn't render a spurious avatar.","startLine":15,"endLine":15,"text":"Don't fake a turn at the cut. Avatar grouping consults the hidden row just above the cut (beforeWindow), so a mid-turn cut doesn't render a spurious avatar."},{"markdown":"Expansion adds a budget of extra rows while following the latest output. Scrolling up pins the first mounted message by ID, preserving the text being read as new rows arrive; returning to the bottom resumes the sliding window. Each button click derives its budget from the effective cut so a tool-run adjustment cannot prevent progress.","startLine":17,"endLine":17,"text":"Expansion adds a budget of extra rows while following the latest output. Scrolling up pins the first mounted message by ID, preserving the text being read as new rows arrive; returning to the bottom resumes the sliding window. Each button click derives its budget from the effective cut so a tool-run adjustment cannot prevent progress."},{"markdown":"New streamed rows cannot unmount the older message being read. The history boundary stays pinned until the reader returns to the bottom, where the normal window budget applies again.","startLine":21,"endLine":21,"text":"New streamed rows cannot unmount the older message being read. The history boundary stays pinned until the reader returns to the bottom, where the normal window budget applies again."},{"markdown":"A pinned boundary is not repeatedly nudged backward through a long tool run.","startLine":23,"endLine":23,"text":"A pinned boundary is not repeatedly nudged backward through a long tool run."},{"markdown":"Unresolved approval and clarification cards remain mounted even when later output exceeds the normal window. Resolving a card releases that exception so old controls can collapse with history.","startLine":27,"endLine":27,"text":"Unresolved approval and clarification cards remain mounted even when later output exceeds the normal window. Resolving a card releases that exception so old controls can collapse with history."},{"markdown":"Scrolling near the top marker auto-reveals the next window (IntersectionObserver, 300px top rootMargin); the button stays as a fallback. A pre-paint `scrollTop` adjustment keeps the content being read in place when rows are prepended.","startLine":31,"endLine":31,"text":"Scrolling near the top marker auto-reveals the next window (IntersectionObserver, 300px top rootMargin); the button stays as a fallback. A pre-paint scrollTop adjustment keeps the content being read in place when rows are prepended."},{"markdown":"Two timing rules keep this correct:","startLine":33,"endLine":33,"text":"Two timing rules keep this correct:"},{"markdown":"The observer is recreated after every expansion (`extraRows` is an effect dependency). IntersectionObserver only reports *transitions*, so after revealing content shorter than the rootMargin (e.g. a tool run folding into one collapsed group) a persistent observer would go silent; re-observing delivers a fresh initial entry.","startLine":35,"endLine":35,"text":"The observer is recreated after every expansion (extraRows is an effect dependency). IntersectionObserver only reports transitions, so after revealing content shorter than the rootMargin (e.g. a tool run folding into one collapsed group) a persistent observer would go silent; re-observing delivers a fresh initial entry."},{"markdown":"History loads scroll to the bottom **instantly**, not smoothly ([[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useChatScroll.ts#useChatScroll]]). A smooth multi-frame scroll from the top races the observer's first callback (the marker is still in view), and the expansion's scroll restore would abort the smooth scroll and strand the view mid-transcript.","startLine":36,"endLine":36,"text":"History loads scroll to the bottom instantly, not smoothly (src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useChatScroll.ts#useChatScroll). A smooth multi-frame scroll from the top races the observer's first callback (the marker is still in view), and the expansion's scroll restore would abort the smooth scroll and strand the view mid-transcript."},{"markdown":"Windowing behavior is specified by [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/MessageList.test.tsx]].","startLine":38,"endLine":38,"text":"Windowing behavior is specified by src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/MessageList.test.tsx."},{"markdown":"Following output is reader intent, not a fresh distance check after every layout change. The chat stays at the latest output until the reader scrolls upward, and offers an explicit return control.","startLine":42,"endLine":42,"text":"Following output is reader intent, not a fresh distance check after every layout change. The chat stays at the latest output until the reader scrolls upward, and offers an explicit return control."},{"markdown":"[[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useChatScroll.ts#useChatScroll]] observes both the viewport and the block-flow transcript wrapper. Streaming commits and asynchronous media, folding, viewport, and content-visibility layout changes schedule at most one animation-frame write using the latest container dimensions. History loads still jump instantly before transcript expansion observers run. Programmatic streaming writes are instant rather than smooth, so intermediate animation positions cannot falsely disable follow.","startLine":44,"endLine":44,"text":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useChatScroll.ts#useChatScroll observes both the viewport and the block-flow transcript wrapper. Streaming commits and asynchronous media, folding, viewport, and content-visibility layout changes schedule at most one animation-frame write using the latest container dimensions. History loads still jump instantly before transcript expansion observers run. Programmatic streaming writes are instant rather than smooth, so intermediate animation positions cannot falsely disable follow."},{"markdown":"A growing row can increase the bottom distance without changing row count or scroll position; that alone does not revoke following. Upward scrolling or upward wheel/keyboard input pauses it, including small movements inside the bottom tolerance. Only downward re-entry within that threshold, submitting a new user turn, or pressing Jump to latest resumes it. Editing navigation keys inside input, textarea, select or contenteditable controls retain their editor behavior. The wrapper retains existing block flow and history-window ancestors, with the return control outside the observed content so showing it cannot change transcript height. It uses the English resource with the existing locale fallback policy.","startLine":46,"endLine":46,"text":"A growing row can increase the bottom distance without changing row count or scroll position; that alone does not revoke following. Upward scrolling or upward wheel/keyboard input pauses it, including small movements inside the bottom tolerance. Only downward re-entry within that threshold, submitting a new user turn, or pressing Jump to latest resumes it. Editing navigation keys inside input, textarea, select or contenteditable controls retain their editor behavior. The wrapper retains existing block flow and history-window ancestors, with the return control outside the observed content so showing it cannot change transcript height. It uses the English resource with the existing locale fallback policy."},{"markdown":"Only an empty transcript gives its wrapper a definite viewport height, preserving the existing empty Chat centering. Message-bearing content keeps natural block height so resize observation detects growth; the new wrapper does not reintroduce a flex transcript layout.","startLine":48,"endLine":48,"text":"Only an empty transcript gives its wrapper a definite viewport height, preserving the existing empty Chat centering. Message-bearing content keeps natural block height so resize observation detects growth; the new wrapper does not reintroduce a flex transcript layout."},{"markdown":"Actual hook tests simulate native intermediate smooth-scroll events and successive same-row token updates. The latest coalesced bottom target remains visible rather than leaving the stream at its obsolete animation target.","startLine":52,"endLine":52,"text":"Actual hook tests simulate native intermediate smooth-scroll events and successive same-row token updates. The latest coalesced bottom target remains visible rather than leaving the stream at its obsolete animation target."},{"markdown":"An unchanged message array can gain height asynchronously. Observing content and viewport bounds follows that growth while coalescing repeated notifications into one frame.","startLine":56,"endLine":56,"text":"An unchanged message array can gain height asynchronously. Observing content and viewport bounds follows that growth while coalescing repeated notifications into one frame."},{"markdown":"Intentional upward scrolling preserves the earlier viewport through content growth. Jump to latest resumes following and subsequent resize updates stay pinned.","startLine":60,"endLine":60,"text":"Intentional upward scrolling preserves the earlier viewport through content growth. Jump to latest resumes following and subsequent resize updates stay pinned."},{"markdown":"A reader who scrolls back to the bottom resumes following without needing the return control, preserving native scrollbar behavior.","startLine":64,"endLine":64,"text":"A reader who scrolls back to the bottom resumes following without needing the return control, preserving native scrollbar behavior."},{"markdown":"Conversation, connection, profile, and accepted settings changes establish a fresh scroll scope. Old observers, listeners, and scheduled frames are disconnected or cancelled before new history pinning or unmount.","startLine":68,"endLine":68,"text":"Conversation, connection, profile, and accepted settings changes establish a fresh scroll scope. Old observers, listeners, and scheduled frames are disconnected or cancelled before new history pinning or unmount."},{"markdown":"Upward wheel input can precede its native scroll event. It cancels the pending following frame immediately so a queued layout update cannot defeat the reader's gesture.","startLine":72,"endLine":72,"text":"Upward wheel input can precede its native scroll event. It cancels the pending following frame immediately so a queued layout update cannot defeat the reader's gesture."},{"markdown":"Adding a newly submitted user row resumes following after reading older content, preserving the existing send behavior.","startLine":76,"endLine":76,"text":"Adding a newly submitted user row resumes following after reading older content, preserving the existing send behavior."},{"markdown":"The actual Chat component supplies the viewport and transcript observer refs and scope. Its return control preserves a paused viewport, jumps to the current bottom, disappears when following resumes, and releases its observer on unmount.","startLine":80,"endLine":80,"text":"The actual Chat component supplies the viewport and transcript observer refs and scope. Its return control preserves a paused viewport, jumps to the current bottom, disappears when following resumes, and releases its observer on unmount."},{"markdown":"Small upward wheel or scrollbar movements override the bottom tolerance and remain paused during subsequent output growth. An actual downward return resumes following.","startLine":84,"endLine":84,"text":"Small upward wheel or scrollbar movements override the bottom tolerance and remain paused during subsequent output growth. An actual downward return resumes following."},{"markdown":"Bubbled navigation keys from input, textarea, select and nested contenteditable controls do not revoke following while the reader is editing an answer.","startLine":88,"endLine":88,"text":"Bubbled navigation keys from input, textarea, select and nested contenteditable controls do not revoke following while the reader is editing an answer."},{"markdown":"Upward navigation outside an editing control continues to pause following, retaining native keyboard reading behavior.","startLine":92,"endLine":92,"text":"Upward navigation outside an editing control continues to pause following, retaining native keyboard reading behavior."},{"markdown":"Content-visibility layout can shrink absolute scrollTop while clamping the view at its actual bottom. A subpixel bottom correction retains follow; a small upward reading gap remains paused.","startLine":96,"endLine":96,"text":"Content-visibility layout can shrink absolute scrollTop while clamping the view at its actual bottom. A subpixel bottom correction retains follow; a small upward reading gap remains paused."},{"markdown":"Streaming events arrive many times per second and each `setMessages` costs a window reconciliation, so the dashboard transport applies deltas to the transcript ref synchronously and commits to React once per animation frame at most.","startLine":100,"endLine":100,"text":"Streaming events arrive many times per second and each setMessages costs a window reconciliation, so the dashboard transport applies deltas to the transcript ref synchronously and commits to React once per animation frame at most."},{"markdown":"See [[chat-commands#Streaming source-of-truth ref]] for the ownership rules that make this safe.","startLine":102,"endLine":102,"text":"See chat-commands#Streaming source-of-truth ref for the ownership rules that make this safe."},{"markdown":"Every transcript row (`.chat-message`) sets `content-visibility: auto` with `contain-intrinsic-size: auto 120px`, so the browser skips layout and paint for off-screen rows. That turns a forced reflow from O(all messages) into O(visible rows).","startLine":106,"endLine":106,"text":"Every transcript row (.chat-message) sets content-visibility: auto with contain-intrinsic-size: auto 120px, so the browser skips layout and paint for off-screen rows. That turns a forced reflow from O(all messages) into O(visible rows)."},{"markdown":"The rule lives on `.chat-message` in the renderer stylesheet (`src/renderer/src/assets/main.css`). That class is shared by user/agent bubbles, the reasoning and tool-activity rows, and the typing indicator (see [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/MessageList.tsx]] and [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/MessageRow.tsx]]), so one rule covers every heavy row.","startLine":108,"endLine":108,"text":"The rule lives on .chat-message in the renderer stylesheet (src/renderer/src/assets/main.css). That class is shared by user/agent bubbles, the reasoning and tool-activity rows, and the typing indicator (see src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/MessageList.tsx and src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/MessageRow.tsx), so one rule covers every heavy row."},{"markdown":"The `auto` keyword in `contain-intrinsic-size` makes the browser remember each row's real measured height after it renders once, so the scrollbar and scroll position stay accurate; the `120px` is only the first-paint estimate for never-yet-rendered rows.","startLine":110,"endLine":110,"text":"The auto keyword in contain-intrinsic-size makes the browser remember each row's real measured height after it renders once, so the scrollbar and scroll position stay accurate; the 120px is only the first-paint estimate for never-yet-rendered rows."},{"markdown":"`content-visibility` implies paint containment, which clips anything drawn outside the row's box — including the hover timestamp that sits below the bubble.","startLine":114,"endLine":114,"text":"content-visibility implies paint containment, which clips anything drawn outside the row's box — including the hover timestamp that sits below the bubble."},{"markdown":"The timestamp (`.chat-bubble-time`) used to overflow ~15px below the bubble and would be clipped. It now sits at `bottom: 1px` inside the row's `padding-bottom: 16px`, so it stays visible while still appearing just under the bubble.","startLine":116,"endLine":116,"text":"The timestamp (.chat-bubble-time) used to overflow ~15px below the bubble and would be clipped. It now sits at bottom: 1px inside the row's padding-bottom: 16px, so it stays visible while still appearing just under the bubble."},{"markdown":"Paint containment also makes each row a containing block for `position: fixed` descendants — a fullscreen overlay rendered inline inside a row gets trapped and clipped to the row's box instead of covering the viewport.","startLine":120,"endLine":120,"text":"Paint containment also makes each row a containing block for position: fixed descendants — a fullscreen overlay rendered inline inside a row gets trapped and clipped to the row's box instead of covering the viewport."},{"markdown":"The image zoom lightboxes in [[src/renderer/src/components/MediaImage.tsx]] and [[src/renderer/src/components/AttachmentChip.tsx]] hit exactly this: `.chat-image-preview-backdrop` is `position: fixed; inset: 0`, and rendered inline it appeared as a clipped strip inside the message row. Both now render through `createPortal(…, document.body)`. Any future overlay spawned from within a transcript row must do the same.","startLine":122,"endLine":122,"text":"The image zoom lightboxes in src/renderer/src/components/MediaImage.tsx and src/renderer/src/components/AttachmentChip.tsx hit exactly this: .chat-image-preview-backdrop is position: fixed; inset: 0, and rendered inline it appeared as a clipped strip inside the message row. Both now render through createPortal(…, document.body). Any future overlay spawned from within a transcript row must do the same."},{"markdown":"Both lightboxes share [[src/renderer/src/hooks/useLightboxClose.ts#useLightboxClose]] for Escape handling. It listens in the capture phase and stops propagation because the lightbox is the topmost modal: other overlays (e.g. the FileViewer panel) bind document-level bubble-phase Escape listeners, and without the capture+stop one keypress would close both the lightbox and the panel behind it.","startLine":124,"endLine":124,"text":"Both lightboxes share src/renderer/src/hooks/useLightboxClose.ts#useLightboxClose for Escape handling. It listens in the capture phase and stops propagation because the lightbox is the topmost modal: other overlays (e.g. the FileViewer panel) bind document-level bubble-phase Escape listeners, and without the capture+stop one keypress would close both the lightbox and the panel behind it."},{"markdown":"The scroll container `.chat-messages` is block flow, not a flex column. A flex column measures each child to lay itself out, which defeats `content-visibility` and reports a wrong `scrollHeight`.","startLine":128,"endLine":128,"text":"The scroll container .chat-messages is block flow, not a flex column. A flex column measures each child to lay itself out, which defeats content-visibility and reports a wrong scrollHeight."},{"markdown":"A correct `scrollHeight` matters because [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useChatScroll.ts#useChatScroll]] uses `scrollHeight - scrollTop - clientHeight` to decide whether the view is pinned to the bottom; a wrong value would break auto-scroll.","startLine":130,"endLine":130,"text":"A correct scrollHeight matters because src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useChatScroll.ts#useChatScroll uses scrollHeight - scrollTop - clientHeight to decide whether the view is pinned to the bottom; a wrong value would break auto-scroll."},{"markdown":"The flex `gap` that previously spaced rows is replaced by per-row spacing: `.chat-message` carries `padding-bottom: 16px` (which also provides the timestamp's room), and non-message children that lack it (`.chat-clarify`) carry an equivalent `margin-bottom`. Block flow also moves alignment from `align-self` to `margin-left: auto` for user rows, and the empty state fills height with `min-height: 100%` instead of `flex: 1`.","startLine":132,"endLine":132,"text":"The flex gap that previously spaced rows is replaced by per-row spacing: .chat-message carries padding-bottom: 16px (which also provides the timestamp's room), and non-message children that lack it (.chat-clarify) carry an equivalent margin-bottom. Block flow also moves alignment from align-self to margin-left: auto for user rows, and the empty state fills height with min-height: 100% instead of flex: 1."},{"markdown":"The composer textarea auto-grows to its content. Reading `scrollHeight` to size it forces a layout flush, so it runs once per committed value in a `useLayoutEffect` keyed on the input string, not on every keystroke.","startLine":136,"endLine":136,"text":"The composer textarea auto-grows to its content. Reading scrollHeight to size it forces a layout flush, so it runs once per committed value in a useLayoutEffect keyed on the input string, not on every keystroke."},{"markdown":"In [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/ChatInput.tsx]] every path that changes the value (typing, history recall, voice transcription, and the imperative `setText`/`appendText`) goes through `setInput`, so the layout effect is the single owner of resizing — the other paths only set the caret and focus. Combined with the row-level `content-visibility`, the one measurement per keystroke stays O(visible rows).","startLine":138,"endLine":138,"text":"In src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/ChatInput.tsx every path that changes the value (typing, history recall, voice transcription, and the imperative setText/appendText) goes through setInput, so the layout effect is the single owner of resizing — the other paths only set the caret and focus. Combined with the row-level content-visibility, the one measurement per keystroke stays O(visible rows)."},{"markdown":"The textarea opts out of the app-wide inset focus shadow and brightness filter because `.chat-input-wrapper:focus-within` already provides the composer's visible focus treatment. This avoids a redundant rectangular outline while preserving keyboard focus visibility.","startLine":140,"endLine":140,"text":"The textarea opts out of the app-wide inset focus shadow and brightness filter because .chat-input-wrapper:focus-within already provides the composer's visible focus treatment. This avoids a redundant rectangular outline while preserving keyboard focus visibility."},{"markdown":"Large Agent command catalogs must not make opening, filtering, scrolling, or keyboard navigation proportional to the number of mounted command elements.","startLine":144,"endLine":144,"text":"Large Agent command catalogs must not make opening, filtering, scrolling, or keyboard navigation proportional to the number of mounted command elements."},{"markdown":"[[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/virtualSlashCommands.ts#createSlashCommandVirtualLayout]] converts the filtered catalog into fixed-height category and command rows. The scroll viewport mounts only intersecting rows plus four command-row heights of overscan, found from the ordered layout with a binary search.","startLine":146,"endLine":146,"text":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/slash/virtualSlashCommands.ts#createSlashCommandVirtualLayout converts the filtered catalog into fixed-height category and command rows. The scroll viewport mounts only intersecting rows plus four command-row heights of overscan, found from the ordered layout with a binary search."},{"markdown":"The fixed heights are an invariant shared with the `.slash-menu-item` and `.slash-menu-group-label` styles. Changing either visual height requires updating the corresponding layout constant so calculated scroll positions and the virtual canvas remain accurate.","startLine":148,"endLine":148,"text":"The fixed heights are an invariant shared with the .slash-menu-item and .slash-menu-group-label styles. Changing either visual height requires updating the corresponding layout constant so calculated scroll positions and the virtual canvas remain accurate."},{"markdown":"Arrow-key selection does not query or measure command DOM nodes. [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/ChatInput.tsx]] computes the selected row's offset and adjusts the list scroll position only when that row leaves the viewport, including wraparound from the first command to the last.","startLine":150,"endLine":150,"text":"Arrow-key selection does not query or measure command DOM nodes. src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/ChatInput.tsx computes the selected row's offset and adjusts the list scroll position only when that row leaves the viewport, including wraparound from the first command to the last."},{"markdown":"The searchable name and description are normalized once when the command catalog changes rather than once per command on every keystroke. The virtual canvas uses layout and paint containment, and the modal overlay avoids backdrop blur so opening the palette does not trigger a full-window blur pass.","startLine":152,"endLine":152,"text":"The searchable name and description are normalized once when the command catalog changes rather than once per comma